  // Return 0 to indicate successful completion of the program
  return 0;
}
```
This program uses a base case of 0 and 1, which are the initial numbers in the Fibonacci sequence, and a recursive case where it calls itself with the smaller of the two remaining numbers. The final result is the nth Fibonacci number, which is displayed to the user. The recursive approach calculates the sequence by summing the results of previous function calls, ultimately giving us the desired Fibonacci number. The program concludes by returning 0, signifying that it has executed successfully without errors.
